  "id": "COMPOUND:42636 - PROTEIN:4970",
  "verbalization": "Camelliquercetiside B appears to exert its biological effects through multiple pathways that ultimately target CCRF-HSB-2, a cancer cell line. The evidence suggests that Camelliquercetiside B acts as a target for several molecules, including Neridienone A and Anolobine, which in turn target CCRF-HSB-2. This indicates a potential mechanism of action involving the modulation of cellular pathways that lead to the suppression of CCRF-HSB-2. Additionally, Camelliquercetiside B is also shown to target MIP, which is further targeted by sec-Butyl acetate, (-)-, reinforcing the possibility of a multi-tiered interaction network. The integration of these pathways highlights the complexity of the relationship, with Camelliquercetiside B potentially influencing cellular processes that ultimately lead to the inhibition of CCRF-HSB-2. The evidence supports a mechanistic link, though the exact nature of the interactions remains to be fully elucidated.",
